  "notes": "Used specifically for aircraft leaving the ground. The noun form {離陸|りりく} is commonly used on its own, as in {離陸|りりく}{時間|じかん} (takeoff time). This is the standard aviation term and is also used in news and travel contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {離陸|りりく}{時間|じかん}: takeoff time\n- {離陸|りりく}{準備|じゅんび}: takeoff preparations\n- {離陸|りりく}{直後|ちょくご}: immediately after takeoff\n- {緊急|きんきゅう}{離陸|りりく}: emergency takeoff\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {着陸|ちゃくりく}する: to land — the opposite, when an aircraft touches down\n- {飛|と}び{立|た}つ: to fly off; to take flight — a more literary or general expression, also used for birds\n- {出発|しゅっぱつ}する: to depart — a broader term for departure that applies to any mode of transport",
